        "About",
        "Did you know ...",
        "... that the species name of Viburnum awabuki (pictured) is derived from a Japanese word for its propensity to blow bubbles when exposed to fire?",
        "... that the opening song to the mahjong anime Pon no Michi was sung by a real-life professional mahjong player?",
        "... that Sun Pictures released nearly 20 films between 2008 and 2010, then slowed sharply after a change of government in Tamil Nadu?",
        "... that The Art Newspaper described the art of Heba Zagout as \"steeped in Palestinian culture and folklore\"?",
        "... that, at one point during the Second Intermediate Period, ancient Egypt might have had three ruling dynasties at the same time?",
        "... that Swiss photographer Albert Steiner was captured by Italian border guards and held for three weeks while on a military reconnaissance mission?",
        "... that Prince performed \"Purple Rain\" during the Super Bowl XLI halftime show under pouring rain and purple lights?",
        "... that Santiphab Phomvihane is the son of a former president of Laos, the brother of a former National Assembly president, and the brother of the country's foreign minister?",
